.\" fsck.filsys.1 - part of filsys 1.0.0
.TH FSCK.FILSYS 1 "August 2026" "filsys 1.0.0" "File Format and Disk Utilities"
.SH NAME
fsck.filsys \- check a V7 filesystem on a raw disk image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsck.filsys
.RB [ \-o
.IR block ]
.I image
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsck.filsys
checks a Seventh Edition Unix filesystem inside a disk image: it validates the
superblock, walks the free-block list checking for out-of-range or duplicated
blocks and a non-terminating chain, and walks the i-list checking each inode's
block pointers.
.PP
A Research Unix disk image holds one or more filesystems
.RI ( partitions ),
selected by a partition table that is compiled into the kernel, not stored on
the disk.  By default
.B fsck.filsys
checks the filesystem at block 0 (the first partition); the
.B \-o
option checks a filesystem at a different block offset within the image.
.PP
The exit status is 0 if the filesystem is clean, 1 if errors were found, and 2
on a usage error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " block"
Check the filesystem at
.I block
(512-byte blocks) within the image, instead of block 0.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
fsck.filsys rp06-0.disk           # check the root filesystem
fsck.filsys -o 18392 rp06-0.disk  # check the filesystem at block 18392
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs.filsys (1),
.BR findfs.filsys (1),
.BR mount.filsys (1),
.BR filsys (5),
.BR icheck (8),
.BR dcheck (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the filsys project.
